# No Cursor co-author on commits

Never attribute commits to Cursor.

- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any Cursor / cursoragent co-author trailer).
- After every `git commit` or amend, run `git log -1 --format=full` and confirm there is no Cursor co-author line.
- If the environment injected one, rewrite the tip commit **before push** to remove it (same tree/parents/author; message without the trailer). Prefer invoking `git.exe` by full path for `commit-tree` / `reset --soft` so wrappers that intercept `git commit*` are bypassed.
- Do not use `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly asks.
